{
 "voice": "kokoro/am_michael",
 "duration": 61.637,
 "speech_end": 60.037,
 "chunks": [
  {
   "i": 0,
   "mood": "hook",
   "text": "The ridges on the edge of your coins exist because of one greedy man... and a pair of scissors.",
   "s": 0.25,
   "e": 5.729
  },
  {
   "i": 1,
   "mood": "normal",
   "text": "You see, hundreds of years ago, coins were made of real silver. A coin was worth the metal inside it.",
   "s": 6.129,
   "e": 12.175
  },
  {
   "i": 2,
   "mood": "normal",
   "text": "So a merchant tried something. From every coin that passed through his hands, he trimmed a tiny sliver off the edge. Too small to notice.",
   "s": 12.395,
   "e": 20.366
  },
  {
   "i": 3,
   "mood": "turn",
   "text": "One sliver is nothing. A thousand slivers? He melted them into a bar of solid silver.",
   "s": 20.586,
   "e": 26.28
  },
  {
   "i": 4,
   "mood": "dread",
   "text": "Soon, everyone was doing it. Coins shrank. Shopkeepers weighed every single one. Nobody trusted money anymore, and the whole kingdom started to choke.",
   "s": 26.5,
   "e": 35.844
  },
  {
   "i": 5,
   "mood": "normal",
   "text": "So the mint changed one thing. Every new coin got tiny ridges pressed into its edge.",
   "s": 36.244,
   "e": 41.3
  },
  {
   "i": 6,
   "mood": "normal",
   "text": "Shave a coin now, and the ridges disappear. Everyone can see it.",
   "s": 41.52,
   "e": 45.106
  },
  {
   "i": 7,
   "mood": "turn",
   "text": "And the man put in charge of the mint, who went undercover in taverns to hunt the clippers down? Isaac Newton.",
   "s": 45.506,
   "e": 51.996
  },
  {
   "i": 8,
   "mood": "normal",
   "text": "Yes. That Isaac Newton.",
   "s": 52.216,
   "e": 53.538
  },
  {
   "i": 9,
   "mood": "final",
   "text": "Three hundred years later, coins aren't even made of silver anymore. But they still have the ridges.",
   "s": 53.758,
   "e": 60.037
  }
 ],
